# GRID European Electronic Communications Code Disclosure (EECCD)

**Last Updated: September 19, 2026**

**Applies to:** GRID services provided to eligible customers in the European Economic Area (EEA) and United Kingdom where the European Electronic Communications Code or corresponding UK requirements apply.

This disclosure supplements the GRID Terms of Service.

## 1. Contact Information
GRID support, regulatory, privacy, legal, accessibility, and postal contact information must be established before public publication.

## 2. Description and Scope
GRID is software for organizing and working with games, installations, modifications, mod managers, profiles, tools, configuration, diagnostics, and related gaming or development workflows.

GRID may use Internet connectivity for authentication, account services, provider information, metadata retrieval, connected services, and other online features. GRID does not provide traditional telephone service, SMS service, public switched telephone network connectivity, or a substitute for general-purpose Internet access.

## 3. Quality of Service
GRID does not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation. Performance and availability may depend on Internet connectivity, device capability, operating-system behavior, game and manager updates, third-party platforms, identity providers, hosting services, and other connected services.

Any future service-level commitment will be stated separately.

## 4. Charges and Fees
Any GRID pricing, subscription tier, usage charge, tax, renewal condition, or paid-service term will be disclosed before purchase. This disclosure does not establish a particular price or billing commitment. Third parties may impose separate charges.

## 5. Contract Duration, Renewal, and Termination
The GRID Terms of Service govern the GRID relationship. If automatically renewing paid subscriptions are introduced, the term, renewal interval, cancellation method, and required information will be disclosed before purchase and according to applicable law.

## 6. Emergency Services and Caller Location
GRID does not provide access to emergency telephone numbers such as 112, 999, or 911 and does not provide caller-location functionality. Use an appropriate telephone, carrier, or authorized emergency-communications service for emergencies.

## 7. Accessibility
LIFE Technology LLC intends GRID to be usable by a broad range of users and will provide accessibility information and assistance consistent with applicable requirements. Accessibility contact information and alternative-format procedures must be established before public publication.

